articles.description:
Dev.to offers both unauthenticated and authenticated APIs, enabling you to fetch public articles or access private data like your own drafts & stats.
You can access public user articles using simple GET requests—no authentication needed:
// Fetch public posts by username
const res = await fetch(`https://dev.to/api/articles?username=yourname`);
const articles = await res.json();
console.log(articles);

Returns an array of public articles with metadata like id, title, description, url, tag_list, etc.
No auth headers required.
Ideal for displaying any user's public posts on your site.
To fetch your private or additional data like drafts or analytics:
Generate an API key on Dev.to Settings → Extensions → DEV Community API Keys

